{
 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.32,
   "text": "Delete Obsidian, because Clod just solved its biggest problem and built itself a second"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.32,
   "end": 3.62,
   "text": "brain."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.06,
   "end": 7.18,
   "text": "This is insane because it now automatically remembers your projects and preferences across"
  },
  {
   "start": 7.18,
   "end": 8.34,
   "text": "every single conversation."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.54,
   "end": 11.14,
   "text": "If you use Clod, you know how annoying it is when it keeps forgetting important"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.14,
   "end": 12.54,
   "text": "details every time you switch chats."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.72,
   "end": 16.0,
   "text": "Now, Clod saves details dynamically in the background, so you can go into your settings"
  },
  {
   "start": 16.0,
   "end": 18.02,
   "text": "and literally see your memories categorized by topic."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.26,
   "end": 21.06,
   "text": "You can click on any file to edit the details or delete anything you want it to"
  },
  {
   "start": 21.06,
   "end": 21.34,
   "text": "forget."
  },
  {
   "start": 22.26,
   "end": 26.48,
   "text": "It even works in your browser across the desktop app and even on mobile for all users."
  },
  {
   "start": 26.66,
   "end": 29.56,
   "text": "This completely changes how you use Clod, but there's one major catch you need"
  },
  {
   "start": 29.56,
   "end": 30.64,
   "text": "know before you turn this on."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.98,
   "end": 33.72,
   "text": "If you say you're tasked to run locally on your machine, the memory won't sync because"
  },
  {
   "start": 33.72,
   "end": 34.7,
   "text": "it only works in the cloud."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.98,
   "end": 36.02,
   "text": "Comment MEM for the free setup."
  }
 ],
